    <DataNode elementId="Alkanes" textLabel="an alkane" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="18310" dataSource="ChEBI" />
      <Graphics centerX="1600.0" centerY="832.5984497070312" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">Alkanes are saturated acyclic hydrocarbons. They consist only of hydrogen and saturated carbon atoms and are bonded exclusively by single bonds. They could be either branched or unbranched. Alkanes are often classified by the length of their acyl moiety. |FRAME: Short-Chain-Alkanes &quot;Short-chain alkanes&quot;| contain less than 6- carbons. |FRAME: Medium-Chain-Alkanes &quot;Medium-chain alkanes&quot;| contain 6-12 carbons. |FRAME: Long-Chain-Alkanes &quot;Long-chain alkanes&quot;| contain 13-22 carbons. |FRAME: Very-Long-Chain-Alkanes &quot;Very-long-chain alkanes&quot;| contain 23 carbons or longer.</Comment>
